# novadeck /etc/os-release (Phase 4c).
#
# Installed as /etc/os-release by images/customize-base.sh. Overriding in /etc is what
# os-release(5) defines /etc for; /usr/lib/os-release stays as the `filesystem` package
# shipped it, so nothing is edited in place and no package file is silently modified.
#
# WHY WE OWN THIS. Before 4c the root was `docker export` of the vendor image, and its
# hand-written /etc/os-release came along — so the image identified itself as "Holo core
# Aarch64 port (preview)", ID=holo-core, with the vendor's VERSION_ID and BUILD_ID. That was
# never true of what we ship, and it is one of the three identity files no package owns (the
# others being /etc/locale.conf and /etc/hostname), so a from-packages bootstrap has to
# answer for it rather than inherit it.
#
# NO PER-BUILD FIELDS. This file is static so that rebuilding does not churn the tree. The
# per-build identity — variant and build timestamp — is written by
# images/assemble-rootfs.sh to /etc/novadeck-release, which is where anything wanting to
# know which image is running should look.
#
# ID_LIKE=arch is load-bearing for third-party tooling that branches on distro family
# (Arch-style paths and package names are what this actually is). ID is ours.

NAME="novadeck"
PRETTY_NAME="novadeck"
ID=novadeck
ID_LIKE=arch
ANSI_COLOR="1;35"
HOME_URL="https://github.com/Nova-Deck/os-build"
